# ONEKA AI — Data Layer Environment Variables
#
# The data module reads DATABASE_URL from backend/.env via python-dotenv.
# In most cases you do NOT need a separate data/.env — the data layer
# inherits its database connection from the backend env file.
#
# Reference: data/db.py loads `backend/.env` automatically:
#   load_dotenv(_REPO_ROOT / "backend" / ".env")
#
# Only create data/.env if you need to override the backend/.env values
# for standalone scraper development (e.g. pointing at a separate test DB).
#
# Copy this file to data/.env and uncomment any variables you want to override.

# ── Database (shared with backend) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Override DATABASE_URL only if you want the data layer to use a different
# database than the backend (e.g. a local dev/test instance).
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://oneka_user:password@localhost:5432/oneka_dev

# ── Scraper behaviour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Maximum pages to scrape per run (eGP, NCA) — lower for faster dev cycles
# EGP_MAX_PAGES=5
# NCA_MAX_PAGES=10

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Playwright scrapers (eGP, NCA, COB) require Chromium to be installed:
#   venv-data/bin/python -m playwright install chromium
#
# The IntelligentCoBParser uses the OPENAI_API_KEY set in backend/.env.
# No OpenAI key is needed in data/.env — it is read server-side by
# backend/src/services/financial_service.py via Pydantic Settings.
